# Chess Coach — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values. `.env.local` is
# gitignored. Vite only exposes variables prefixed with `VITE_` to the
# browser, which is why every public key here is `VITE_*`.
#
# See SETUP_AUTH.md for the click-by-click setup that produces these.

# Clerk — Publishable key (safe to ship to the browser).
# Found at: dashboard.clerk.com → your app → API Keys → "Publishable key".
# Starts with `pk_test_` (development) or `pk_live_` (production).
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Supabase — project URL.
# Found at: supabase.com/dashboard → your project → Project Settings → API → "Project URL".
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=

# Supabase — publishable key (safe to ship to the browser).
# New format: starts with `sb_publishable_...`. Older projects may have an
# `anon public` JWT key starting with `eyJhbGc...` — use that if it's all
# the dashboard offers; both formats work identically.
# DO NOT use the service_role / secret key — it bypasses RLS.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ── NNUE network host (production only) ─────────────────────────────────
#
# Where the browser fetches Stockfish's 38.3 MiB NNUE network from.
#
# LEAVE THIS UNSET LOCALLY. Unset means same-origin: `npm run dev` stages the
# net into `public/stockfish/` and the app loads it from there — no external
# dependency, works offline, and it is what the test suite expects.
#
# You normally do not set this by hand at all. `npm run nnue:setup` stands up the
# R2 bucket and writes the value to `.env.production`, which is committed and is
# what production builds read. Vite ignores `.env.production` in dev, so `npm run
# dev` keeps using the locally staged net.
#
# Set it HERE (or in the Cloudflare Pages environment) only to override that —
# a real environment variable outranks the file. Format:
#
#   VITE_NNUE_NET_URL=https://pub-<hash>.r2.dev
#
# The host MUST send `Access-Control-Allow-Origin`. Nothing else is required —
# not `Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy`, despite the app being cross-origin
# isolated. Verify a configured host with:
#
#   npm run nnue:upload -- --verify-only
#
# A misconfigured host does not just make evals worse, it makes Stockfish exit
# mid-search; the app's HEAD probe is what turns that into a labelled fallback
# to the classical evaluator. See DEPLOY.md § The NNUE network.
VITE_NNUE_NET_URL=
